      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That is a common paranoid thought, but most standard ergonomic chairs simply measure pressure points to adjust lumbar support and do not contain biometric sensors capable of tracking heart rate or detailed focus levels. Since there is no scientific evidence of such advanced tracking technology in these products, you likely don't need to mask your signals at all. It is generally better to simply trust your company's hardware and ignore the conspiracy rather than worrying about unproven surveillance tools.",
